From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hfp_ag: end the +CNUM reply with the service field

The Hands-Free spec has the gateway answer AT+CNUM with
+CNUM: ,"number",type,,service, where service is 4 for voice. BTstack sent
the speed and service as empty, space-padded fields (`,129, , `), which its
own hands-free parser takes but Bluedroid's does not: it matches the two
commas and the service number together, so the reply was dropped and the
headset never saw the number. The line also had room for only 28 digits of the 32 the spec allows.

diff --git a/src/classic/hfp_ag.c b/src/classic/hfp_ag.c
--- a/src/classic/hfp_ag.c
+++ b/src/classic/hfp_ag.c
@@ -241,8 +241,8 @@
 }
 
 static int hfp_send_subscriber_number_cmd(uint16_t cid, uint8_t type, const char * number){
-    char buffer[50];
-    snprintf(buffer, sizeof(buffer), "\r\n%s: ,\"%s\",%u, , \r\n",
+    char buffer[64];
+    snprintf(buffer, sizeof(buffer), "\r\n%s: ,\"%s\",%u,,4\r\n",
              HFP_SUBSCRIBER_NUMBER_INFORMATION, number, type);
     buffer[sizeof(buffer) - 1] = 0;
     return send_str_over_rfcomm(cid, buffer);
